# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: deferred-nod-default-contents -- what cador leaves out of the vendors' default objects and of saving them
#+STATUS: OPEN
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: feature
#+DEPENDS: cador-entget-subclass-layout-and-record-pointers
#+BRANCH: -
#+DATE: 2026-10-24

* Context

clautolisp 2.3.52 (cador-entget-subclass-layout-and-record-pointers, items
3-5) gave table records handles, TABLE owners and the BLOCK / BLOCK_RECORD
split, and filled a fresh drawing's named-object dictionary with each
product's default entries (entget-pointers section 11: AutoCAD 2022 job
17439813490, BricsCAD V26 job 17439813492, V25 job 17439813491). It made
only what those measurements reach: the containers, ACAD_PLOTSTYLENAME's
Normal placeholder and ACAD_MATERIAL's ByBlock / ByLayer / Global.

* Deferred

1. Dictionary contents the vendors have and cador does not: ACAD_LAYOUT's
   Model / Layout1 LAYOUT objects, ACAD_MLINESTYLE / ACAD_TABLESTYLE /
   ACAD_MLEADERSTYLE Standard, ACAD_SCALELIST's scales, ACAD_VISUALSTYLE's
   styles, AcDbVariableDictionary's variables. Each needs measuring first:
   entget-pointers section 12 dumps them (MR !484).
2. The MATERIAL objects' full group lists (about 100 groups on both CADs)
   and ACDBPLACEHOLDER / RASTERVARIABLES / MENTALRAYRENDERSETTINGS bodies:
   cador shows the type, marker and name only.
3. AutoCAD's extension dictionaries ({ACAD_XDICTIONARY 360}) on the layer
   record and the TABLE objects, the layer's 348, BricsCAD's BLOCK 71, the
   BLOCK_RECORD's 360 / 340 / {BLKREFS 331 ...} groups.
4. Saving them: the DXF writer puts every object of the entities table in
   ENTITIES (a pre-existing limit for entmade dictionaries and xrecords too)
   and writes only the legacy struct dictionary tree in OBJECTS; a
   DXF-loaded drawing's NOD is not what (namedobjdict) reaches. The
   handle-addressed objects should go to OBJECTS, and a loaded NOD become
   the handle-addressed one.
